    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d524">

                <pb facs="0533" n="525" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg525"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51 Public Works Debt/214</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1880</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-04-18">April 18,
                        1939</date>.<lb/>[Received April 19.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In continuation of previous correspondence
                    concerning the settlement of the Public Works Debt, I have the honor to enclose
                    here-with <pb facs="0534" n="526" xml:id="pg526"/> a memorandum of my
                    conversation with the President of the Republic on the 17th instant in further
                    relation thereto—from which it will appear that the President is now of the
                    opinion that the legislation as originally drafted will soon be passed by the
                    Cuban Congress.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Butler Wright</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d524-a1.xml" xpointer="d524-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
